   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalUpsilon]", "r"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "967c7c3a-83ea-4f37-a262-7a32e2bb7bc5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalUpsilon]", "\[Phi]"], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"7b0a826b-3174-45c2-be86-41b01fcf3053"],
 " . \nNotice that the frequencies shifts (and their geodesics counterparts) \
for periodic orbits will converge logarithmically to the homoclinic \
frequencies  for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["r", 
     RowBox[{"3", "g"}]], "->", 
    SubscriptBox["r", 
     RowBox[{"2", "g"}]]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "94f82bfe-5932-4fe6-942b-63832abdc779"],
 ". As such, the convergence is pretty slow, and one needs to be very closed \
to the separatrix for periodic orbits to observe the convergence numerically. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.931530932025839*^9, 3.931531003498089*^9}, {
   3.936069763733927*^9, 3.9360697824728117`*^9}, 3.967780154912736*^9, {
